<%#
  The end of the run, kept on the transcript.

  The runner this replaced swapped the page for a "Run complete" card, throwing
  away the thing the agent had just been reading. Here the answered steps stay
  where they are and this sits under them; the results page is a link rather
  than a destination the runner forces you to.

  Two endings, because they are not the same news. A run that reached a Resolve
  is finished. A stranded run stopped because the step it was on had branches
  and the answer matched none of them — the agent did nothing wrong and the call
  is not over, so saying "This run is complete" hands them a dead end dressed as
  a result. The wording is for someone on a live call, not for the builder.

  There is no Back here yet: without park the run has already ended. That card
  is the next piece of this work.

  locals: scenario, results_url
%>
<div class="runner-thread__complete">
  <% if scenario.stranded? %>
    <p class="text-sm">This workflow doesn&rsquo;t have a step for that answer, so it stops here.</p>
  <% else %>
    <p class="text-sm">This run is complete.</p>
  <% end %>
  <%= link_to "View results", results_url, class: "btn btn--secondary btn--sm" %>
</div>
